### VS Code REST Client (extension: humao.rest-client) - run against `npm run dev`
@host = http://localhost:3000

### Dashboard state (what the UI polls every 2s)
GET {{host}}/api/state?since=0

### Download blank template / sample test workbook
GET {{host}}/api/template
###
GET {{host}}/api/template?sample=1

### Approved records, searchable + paginated
GET {{host}}/api/records?status=Approved&q=CDS&priority=High&page=1&pageSize=10&sort=ProcessedAt&dir=desc

### Upload (immediate). Replace the path with your filled workbook
POST {{host}}/api/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=X

--X
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="mode"

immediate
--X
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="CleanCore_Defects_SAMPLE_5records.xlsx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet

< ./samples/CleanCore_Defects_SAMPLE_5records.xlsx
--X--

### Approve a record (paste an id from /api/state -> pending[].id)
POST {{host}}/api/records/PASTE-ID-HERE/approve

### Change assignee
POST {{host}}/api/records/PASTE-ID-HERE/reassign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "senior.cfl@smartshift.com", "note": "CFL specialist needed" }

### Cancel a scheduled run
DELETE {{host}}/api/scheduled/PASTE-RUN-ID-HERE

### Export master workbook (all | Approved | "In Progress" | "Changed Assignee")
GET {{host}}/api/export?status=all

### Sync status / force a sync
GET {{host}}/api/sync
###
POST {{host}}/api/sync

### Google Drive storage: connection test (writes state/connection-test.txt)
POST {{host}}/api/sync/test

### Google Drive storage: restore the dashboard from state/store.json in the Drive folder (replaces local store)
POST {{host}}/api/sync/restore

### Open an attachment (set = uploadId from a record's attachments[].setId)
GET {{host}}/api/attachment?set=PASTE-SET-ID&name=st22_cast_dump.png

### Cancel an entry (no Jira ticket will be created; a reason is required)
POST {{host}}/api/records/PASTE-RECORD-ID/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Raised by mistake" }

### Recurrence report by Fix / Rule ID (JSON), and as an Excel download
GET {{host}}/api/report/recurrence
###
GET {{host}}/api/report/recurrence?format=xlsx
